Scenario B: Conflict between Burst Time and Priority

 Input Data:

o P1: Arrival=0, Burst=8, Priority=1 (Long but Urgent)
o P2: Arrival=1, Burst=2, Priority=5 (Short but Not Urgent)

 Description

"This test reveals the policy trade-off.
Priority scheduling ensures P1 finishes first because it is urgent.
However, both SJF versions (Preemptive and Non-Preemptive) prefer P2 to minimize waiting time.
The difference here is that SJF Preemptive will stop P1 immediately at time 1 to run P2,
while Non-Preemptive will make P2 wait until P1 finishes at time 8."
